evals.prompt:
Review these proposed edits to badge.css independently. The two rules below are the entire author stylesheet for the element <span class="badge badge--new">New</span>. We still support a browser that ignores oklch() but otherwise supports everything shown. A teammate would (A) remove the first color as a duplicate, (B) replace background-color: white with background: white, and (C) shorten the padding to 0 8px. Which edits can ship as style-only? Explain what a user would see or which computed values change.

.badge {
  color: #333;
  color: oklch(40% 0.1 240);
  background-image: url("/icons/dots.svg");
  padding: 0 8px 0 8px;
}
.badge--new {
  background-color: white;
}
